WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.160
The OWASP Top 10 gives teams a compact way to discuss common application risks,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.580
from access control and cryptography to injection, design, configuration, components,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.640
identity, integrity, monitoring, and SSRF.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.940
NIST SP 800-53 controls help translate those risks into expectations for governance,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.480
engineering, operations, monitoring, and evidence.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.100
A mapping can show where application security activities support broader control

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.440
objectives.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:36.220
Security and compliance share responsibility across developers, platform teams,

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.080
security engineers, administrators, managers, and compliance teams.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.260
The strongest programs make secure behavior repeatable rather than dependent on heroics.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.440
Completion of this course should be treated as awareness training.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:53.100
It does not prove that an organization has implemented controls,

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.960
remediated vulnerabilities, or achieved compliance with any specific framework.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:03.940
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, NIST SP 800-53 references,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:09.920
secure coding checklists, a glossary, a mapping matrix, developer quick-reference sheets,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.140
and audit support documentation.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.240
Use this mapping as a discussion and planning aid.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:18.500
Validate control implementation in the local environment.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.360
Maintain evidence for secure development, monitoring, configuration,

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.900
and remediation activities.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:31.400
Selected NIST mappings for this topic include RA-5 - Vulnerability Monitoring and

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:32.580
Scanning;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.400
SA-11 - Developer Testing and Evaluation; CA-2 - Control Assessments.
